      <Description>This dataset contains CIS-CODIF Oxygen+ Pitch-Angle Distribution, for the Low-sensitivity side of spacecraft C4, in Differential_Particle_Flux units.

          The CIS (Cluster Ion Spectrometry) experiment is a comprehensive ionic plasma spectrometry package onboard the Cluster spacecraft, capable of obtaining full three-dimentional ion distributions (about 0 to 40 keV/e) with a time resolution of one spacecraft spin (4 sec) and with mass-per-charge composition determination. The CIS package consists of two different instruments, a time-of-flight ion Composition and Distribution Function analyser (CODIF, or CIS-1) and a Hot Ion Analyser (HIA, or CIS-2).
          </Description>
